 ## Operating characteristics
-**Time and Memory Complexity:**
-*   **Opacity Computation:** One lookup table reference per voxel if gradient magnitudes are pre-stored. New lookup table generation is required if classification parameters change [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Ray Tracing/Compositing:** For a square image of $n$ pixels with orthographic projection and $K$ sample locations along each ray, the cost is $3Kn^2$ additions, $2Kn^2$ tri-linear interpolations, and $Kn^2$ linear interpolations [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+**Time and Memory Complexity:** Opacity computation requires one lookup table reference per voxel if gradient magnitudes are pre-stored; new lookup table generation is required if classification parameters change [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. Ray tracing/compositing cost for a square image of $n$ pixels with orthographic projection and $K$ sample locations along each ray is $3Kn^2$ additions, $2Kn^2$ tri-linear interpolations, and $Kn^2$ linear interpolations [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
 
-**Measured Performance:**
-*   **Molecular Graphics (Cytochrome B5, 113x113x113 voxels):** Classification/shading took 5 minutes on a SUN 4/280 with 32MB RAM. Ray tracing/compositing took 40 minutes [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Medical Imaging (CT Cadaver, 113 slices of 256x256):** Computation of each set of colors/opacities took 20 minutes. Each view/compositing took an additional 20 minutes [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+**Measured Performance:** In a molecular graphics study (Cytochrome B5 electron density map, 113x113x113 voxels), classification/shading took 5 minutes on a SUN 4/280 with 32MB RAM, and ray tracing/compositing took 40 minutes [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. In a medical imaging study (CT cadaver, 113 slices of 256x256), computation of each set of colors/opacities took 20 minutes, and each view/compositing took an additional 20 minutes [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
 
-**Strengths and Limitations:**
-*   **Strengths:** Renders thin, wispy surfaces instead of holes for regions not meeting strict adjacency or threshold criteria. Suppresses tissue interiors while enhancing bounding surfaces. Carries 3-D bandlimiting into 2-D projection, reducing aliasing [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires adjacency criteria to be met for unambiguous classification. Sensitive to acquisition artifacts (striping from anisotropy or motion). Blurring opacities softens silhouettes but may reduce sharpness. Super-sampling substantially increases computational expense [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
