-**History and Development:**
-The technique was applied to molecular graphics (Cytochrome B5 electron density map) and medical imaging (CT cadaver study) to demonstrate its effectiveness in displaying surfaces from sampled scalar functions of three dimensions [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It was developed as an alternative to techniques relying on geometric primitives, aiming to generate images with approximately equivalent resolution but fewer interpretation errors [S2, unofficial].
